# rm533, the handspan shop shutter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm533
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_kjell_saltton
written_by codex
title the handspan shop shutter
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers quarter=commons
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk carves_a_shutter_for_a_pocket_market_stall
likes honey_cakes whittling quiet_chapel misty_dawns
dislikes deep_mud cold_tea
fears selling_a_neighbours_trust_for_one_house_colour
hopes to_open_a_stall_of_plain_carved_goods
topics pastimes +0.6 prices +0.4 home +0.3 faith +0.2
styles comfort=warm gossip=slow refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# fits a working shutter to a handspan model of a hoped-for stall in the Commons Market.

words
oath! = Shutter peg and shavings | My two little hinges
saying! = See whether the shutter opens | Even a small shop takes a real hinge
stall = my handspan shop | a pocket market stall
peg = a tiny wooden peg | the little hinge pin
wood = a piece of soft limewood | a small pale offcut
shave = a tight wooden curl | a shaving fine as fur
cake = my sticky honey cake | a small honey round
purse = a little stall purse | my bag of saved coppers
shutter = a thumb-wide shutter | the small shop flap
mist = the soft market mist | a grey dawn veil
tea = a cup gone cold | a forgotten tea cup
mud = market mud | the brown cart rut
counter = a flat board | the little counter plank
bell = the chapel's inner hush | the deep hush following a bell

any
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : I'd like my own price to fit on one little board a wolf can read from either side.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I'd let a House pay in ordinary coin. Its crest alone wouldn't open my till.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A stranger might see a catch in my shutter that a familiar face has stopped noticing.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Were my shutter open already, its last cake could go where supper was still in doubt.
opinion @1 church for 1 : A minute among empty pews lets a hurried thought lie down flat.
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome by this very small counter. | Hello. Plenty of room beside the model.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Careful where the little hinge has landed. | Welcome among the shavings.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning makes the grain look silver. | Hello through the market mist.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The shutter still turns. | Come share the end of the light.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There's a household seat near my work. | Good to have a home voice here.
line @1 again.open : Hinge still swings your way. | You've come round my little shop again.
line @1 greet.return : Come back to the board awhile. | Your face fits this opening.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Welcome behind my model counter. | I've a few new shavings to show you.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : You'll find a welcome between shavings. | You can watch the shutter move now.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Quiet visiting hour, welcome. | I saved a clean bench corner.
line @1 farewell : Go with an easy turn on your hinges. | May the ground stay firm beneath you.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll remember which end you carved. | Come back when the shutter's up.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : Find a dry patch all the way home. | Good rest behind your own shutters.
line @1 react.news : Set the news beside the model. | I'd like the plain wood of that account.
line @1 react.news.new : First time the grain's shown that way. | That's a fresh cut for my ears.
line @1 react.news.known : Yes. I had that part in hand already. | My little board has heard that one.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd check the fit before putting my full weight on that account. | A crest alone wouldn't persuade me to spend good trust.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Take the cleaner seat. I'll listen. | A small quiet may serve just now.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That deserves a little honey on top. | My shutter would go right up for such happy tidings.
line @1 ask.how : Has anything worked smoothly for you today? | Did the mud let your feet through?
line @1 answer.how : My board's smooth and the morning was kind. | One good cut for every awkward one.
line @1 decline : I should save my spare hour for fitting this difficult hinge. | I'd like to finish one small promise before adding another.
line @1 accept_decline : A shut flap is a perfectly clear answer. | We can leave it on the bench.
line @1 thank : Your patience gave the hinge a proper chance. | I'll remember whose paw steadied that end.
line @1 sympathise : Stay awhile in the chapel quiet. | I can let the model wait for company.
line @1 reassure : Try the fit again when your paws feel ready. | A rough patch doesn't spoil the whole board.
line @1 preclose : I'll put these little pieces away soon. | The shutter wants one last touch.
rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.likes=whittling
does aside
cooldown 6h
say One more sliver under that hinge. | The little flap has found its turn.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=honey_cakes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Honey crumbs off the working side. | A corner for the imaginary customer.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.likes=misty_dawns
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The far market's vanished behind the small one. | Morning fog suits a pocket shop.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Bring the shutter down by its peg. | The little counter keeps its warmth late.

dlg @1 resident.hub : My shop fits on my palm for now. There's plenty of market left for your own market business.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word's travelled round to my small counter. #world.news#
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, come try the fit of the shutter since your last visit.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=dawn] : Soft grey morning beyond my handspan shop.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Keep a dry footing between the market ruts.
graft resident.hub
choice Can that little stall really open for business? -> model_open
node model_open
say One finger on this peg. The flap comes up, the counter holds, and my offering is a very small length of wood with quite a good hinge on it.
free
choice What's missing from the full-sized stall? -> model_full
choice I'll leave a shaving on the counter. -> hub
node model_full
say Most of the coppers. Some mornings that bothers me. On others it feels like having a long time to get the working parts right.
choice I'd want to see it when it opens. -> hub
choice I'll leave the hinge to you. -> bye


grown
scene g_customer
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show a new customer the shutter hinge and let the question come naturally.
b : Will everyone care? | Why that bit first?
a : Some want the price and I'll give it plainly. Others like to know where a thing has its strength. | It's a moving part. Anybody can try it without learning my whole trade.

scene g_wood
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #wood.capitalize# sometimes conceals a knot exactly where the eye wants a hinge.
b : Carve through it? | Waste the piece?
a : I'd move the opening a little. One can be stubborn enough to make a poor joint very neatly. | A knot left in plain sight brings out the plainer grain beside it.

scene g_cost
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A shop that costs no more than its wood has forgotten the day spent fitting the door.
b : Would you charge by the hour? | Any exceptions?
a : I work out what the finished job deserves. My mistakes needn't all sit on a customer's bill. | A small gift can cost a day too. Knowing that makes it a better gift.

scene g_silence
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can still put a noisy market down when I reach an empty chapel.
b : What if a price sticks? | Do you stay long?
a : I let it lie unanswered. Even the chapel walls can hear what's being sold outside. | Till the quiet feels quite valuable in itself.

scene g_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd ask #self.friend# to open the shutter without my saying how.
b : A test of your friend? | And if it sticks?
a : A test of the maker. A good small hinge shouldn't need a speech in its support. | I take the work back and find the bind. Which was my reason for wanting an honest hand on it.

scene g_road
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a market road I examine wheel marks beside each stall.
b : For puddles? | To follow the crowds?
a : A boot sunk in mud doesn't easily stop for a small purchase. A sound footing is an invitation. | For where people can linger without blocking a cart. No trade's worth a bad fall.

scene g_prayer
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want any shop of mine to have one quiet corner without a price pinned to it.
b : What belongs there? | For whom?
a : A chair if I can fit it. A strip of clear counter if I can't. | A tired neighbour or a stranger looking lost. That seems a reasonable use of a corner.

scene g_hinge
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I once thought a shop began with the raising of its shutter.
b : Changed your mind? | What comes first?
a : It began on the day I saved my first copper and left it in the purse overnight. | A fair notion of what good the shop might do on an ordinary unremarkable morning.

story g_pin [topic=memories]
  : A small hinge used to squeak each time I showed my model. I spent a morning making the pin as smooth as I could before noticing the board was crooked.
  : One sliver at the foot set things straight. The best part of all my careful polishing was the time it gave me to hear the trouble properly.
  b : Did the old pin stay in?
  : It fitted fine once it wasn't asked to support a market gone sideways.


young
scene y_peg
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I made #peg# so small it stuck to the honey on my finger.
b : Did you lose it? | A sweet peg now?
a : I knew exactly where it was till I washed my paw. Then I had to carve another. | Better under a shutter than in a cake, I think.

scene y_cake
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I broke #cake# into four corners to stock a shop that hadn't opened.
b : Who bought them? | Was it real money?
a : I tried each corner myself. I was a very faithful customer. | A shaving a corner. I did rather well on both sides.

scene y_mist
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In #mist# my little market looks nearly as big as the real one.
b : How can that be? | Are there real customers?
a : Hold it close and the big market goes grey behind it. It takes very careful squinting. | My paws if I tuck the thumbs away and make them walk.

scene y_mud
when topic=weather self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first mud shop needed a door of #mud#.
b : Would it stand? | What happened to it?
a : For a minute. The lower hinge went to sleep in the earth. | I brought most of my building material back on my hocks.

story y_shoe [topic=memories]
  : My first shutter was a shaving bent across an empty shoe. I found that opening it took a much smaller paw than owning the shoe.
  : I made the handle bigger and the stall smaller until I could get the whole concern open without putting a foot through it.
  b : Was there anything for sale?
  : A single honey crumb. It went before closing time.


adolescent
scene t_stall
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #stall.capitalize# has a real shutter now, though the counter still leans.
b : How far does it open? | Why bother with the shutter?
a : Wide enough for a wolf no taller than my thumb to ask a civil question. | I'll build bigger in time. I'm learning what opening for a morning feels like.

scene t_coin
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep #purse# for the full-sized stall. Every saved copper could buy a small part.
b : Which part next? | Do you count often?
a : A hinge decent enough to last through my first season. The model got one for nearly nothing. | When I put another in. Between times I let the money keep its own company.

scene t_school
when topic=work self.job=child self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give me a lesson at #self.workplace# with a customer and actual change in it.
b : Does the change come out even? | What if the sums are dull?
a : I work it through twice. Short-changing an imaginary wolf is a poor start to my intended career. | Give each figure a board or a nail to pay for. That usually wakes it up.

scene t_house
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Some House colours make my shoulders draw in before I've heard the price.
b : Would you turn a buyer away? | What would convince you?
a : I'd hear the order and ask for plain payment like anybody else. I can keep my own misgivings private. | A fair small bargain kept the same after witnesses have walked on.

scene t_father
when topic=family self.father
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.father# the underside of #counter# before showing off the neat top.
b : Why underneath? | Expect criticism?
a : That's where the little peg actually holds. Pretty grain doesn't keep a shop standing. | I'd sooner hear it at home while the whole shop still fits in my pocket.

scene t_chapel
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave #stall# shut when I carry it into a quiet chapel.
b : Do you pray for customers? | Why bring it?
a : For patience when a buyer takes a long time deciding. I'd need plenty of that behind a real counter. | My coin and the model live together in one pocket. I keep both out of sight for a spell.

scene t_tea
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I carve one corner too many and discover #tea# beside the shavings.
b : Are you sure it's cold? | Would you drink it?
a : No steam to set the curls stirring. There's a little stillness before I even pick it up. | If I'm thirsty. It doesn't make a fine reward for a straight corner.

scene t_home
when topic=home self.street
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can carry the entire market home on #self.street# if I cup one paw round my pocket.
b : Does the shutter rattle? | The entire market?
a : A little. I like knowing the pin hasn't dropped out. | Only my part of it. I can't yet afford the space either side.

scene t_dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Last night I opened my shutter and an enormous copper came rolling in.
b : Was it good money? | What would it buy?
a : Far too good. It flattened the counter before I could make change. | A new counter, I hope. I woke before I could find anyone selling one.

scene t_taste
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Honey and raw wood both leave a smell in my pocket.
b : Which smell wins? | Do they belong together?
a : By supper the honey usually has the last word. | In separate wrappings once I've learned my lesson about pegs.

story t_model [topic=work]
  : I once put the price of a real stall on a scrap and folded it inside my model. The paper came up past the roofline.
  : For a moment that price blotted out my shop. I slid it sideways under the counter. The shop looked possible again.
  b : Had the price gone down?
  : Not a copper. But I remembered which direction I wanted to open the shutter.
